# Docker build context exclusions for this repository.
#
# Both images are built from the repository root:
#   docker build -f backend/Dockerfile  -t local-ai-harness-backend:local  .
#   docker build -f frontend/Dockerfile -t local-ai-harness-frontend:local .
# so this single root file is the one Docker reads (files in subdirectories are
# ignored when the context is the repository root).
#
# Patterns use `**/` so nested locations (backend/, frontend/) are matched too.

# Dependency and build output: always recreated inside the images.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Test output.
**/coverage

# Test sources are not build inputs for production images (Step 24.1).
# Test-only helpers that do not match this pattern may still be present; that
# is acceptable and keeps the packaging simple.
**/*.test.ts

# Environment files: never bake .env contents (or future secrets) into layers.
**/.env*

# Logs.
**/logs
**/*.log

# Temporary upload data.
**/uploads
**/temp
/tmp

# Version control.
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Editor / OS artifacts.
.vscode
.idea
**/.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
**/*.swp
**/*.swo

# npm lockfile kept next to the authoritative pnpm-lock.yaml; the images use
# pnpm only. Excluded from the context (not deleted from the repository).
package-lock.json

# Intentionally NOT ignored, because the builds require them:
#   package.json, backend/package.json, frontend/package.json,
#   pnpm-lock.yaml, pnpm-workspace.yaml, backend/tsconfig.json,
#   frontend/tsconfig*.json, backend/src, frontend/src, frontend/index.html,
#   frontend/public, frontend/vite.config.ts, backend/Dockerfile,
#   frontend/Dockerfile, frontend/nginx.conf
